From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] win32u: a process takes the display scale handed to it in SG_LOGPIXELS

The system DPI comes from the account's LogPixels, read once as the
process starts. sg-session starts the login screen, Setup on the live
medium and the first-run setup -- programs Wine scales, of an account that
never chooses a scale -- at the screen's recommended scale (David
2026-10-05, a Surface Pro 7 at 2736x1824: they were a small box in the
middle of the screen). It first did that by writing LogPixels with wine
reg as the greeter's account just before starting the greeter: Wine
processes on the shared system prefix ahead of the login screen, which
the release's boot test could not afford. The scale is now handed to the
process in its environment instead: SG_LOGPIXELS, 96 to 480, is taken
over the registry's for the system DPI and the fonts' DPI; nothing is
written. Unset (every session, every other program) nothing changes.

Test: test/logpixelsenv-gate.sh with test/logpixelsenv-probe.c (mutant
SG_MUTANT_NO_LOGPIXELS_ENV); sg-session's test/hidpi-ui-e2e.sh.
---
--- a/dlls/win32u/sysparams.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/sysparams.c
@@ -5469,6 +5469,20 @@
         }
     }
     if (!system_dpi) system_dpi = USER_DEFAULT_SCREEN_DPI;
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_NO_LOGPIXELS_ENV
+    /* Stained Glass OS: the display scale handed to this process by the one
+     * that started it (SG_LOGPIXELS), over the account's: the login screen,
+     * Setup and the first-run setup are started at the screen's recommended
+     * scale (sg-session sg-ui-scale) without anything written to the
+     * registry beforehand -- a Wine process run for that, as the greeter's
+     * account, before the greeter left it without its X connection
+     * (2026-10-05). */
+    {
+        const char *env = getenv( "SG_LOGPIXELS" );
+        UINT dpi = env ? strtoul( env, NULL, 10 ) : 0;
+        if (dpi >= USER_DEFAULT_SCREEN_DPI && dpi <= 480) system_dpi = dpi;
+    }
+#endif
 
     /* FIXME: what do the DpiScalingVer flags mean? */
     get_dword_entry( (union sysparam_all_entry *)&entry_DPISCALINGVER, 0, &dpi_scaling, 0 );
--- a/dlls/win32u/font.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/font.c
@@ -4928,6 +4928,15 @@
         NtClose( key );
     }
     if (!dpi) dpi = 96;
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_NO_LOGPIXELS_ENV
+    /* Stained Glass OS: the display scale handed down (SG_LOGPIXELS), as
+     * sysparams.c takes it */
+    {
+        const char *env = getenv( "SG_LOGPIXELS" );
+        UINT env_dpi = env ? strtoul( env, NULL, 10 ) : 0;
+        if (env_dpi >= 96 && env_dpi <= 480) dpi = env_dpi;
+    }
+#endif
 
     font_gamma_ramp.gamma = gamma;
     TRACE( "gamma %d screen dpi %u\n", font_gamma_ramp.gamma, dpi );
